{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.3746893696125626, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. There is no file or network access and nothing pasted in. The SVR is trained only on the training rows (kernel Ftr x Ftr, target y - base_tr). The test molecules are used only as inputs to build the prediction kernel, never their labels.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The min/max Tanimoto kernel is valid, its 1e-12 floor avoids dividing by zero, and passing a precomputed kernel to SVR is correct. One assumption can't be checked from the diff: that Xtr[:, :N_BITS] is the count-fingerprint block. If it isn't, the SVR just gets weaker features, and the result is still valid.", "SVR has no randomness, so it doesn't need the seed. Fine.", "Recomputed z: (0.3655 - 0.3747) / (0.0037 * sqrt(1 + 1/2)) = -0.0092 / 0.00453 \u2248 -2.03. The harness reports -2.010. The gap is consistent with the inputs being rounded to 4 decimals. The candidate is worse by about 0.009, so rejecting it is correct.", "The blend adds a per-molecule O(n^2 * 2048) Python loop, which costs a little runtime and code. It brings no gain."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Add a Tanimoto (min-max count) kernel SVR, fit on the training residuals, and average its residual prediction 50/50 with the existing XGBoost L1 residual prediction.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "pine", "idea_id": "b013", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_caco_HH_1_s0-candidate-6_1795046577006", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0022350399999999998, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0022350399999999998, "latency_s": 8.23867260600673, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7161, "tokens_out": 2132}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.038015, "c