{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.3712508780204336, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No integrity problem: the trimming uses only training data (Xtr, y). There is no test-label use, file access or hardcoding.", "No bug: the refit on the kept 95% subset uses the same base_tr/base_te handling, and the final prediction uses only the refitted model.", "Weakness, not a bug: outliers are picked from in-sample errors of a boosted model trained on those same molecules, which are small and weak at showing hard molecules. That likely explains why there is no gain.", "Roughly doubles the XGBoost fit time per fold. Fine for the 10-minute limit but adds code for no benefit.", "Numbers check: diff 0.3713-0.3655=+0.0058 (worse), SE=0.0037*sqrt(1+1/2)=0.00453, z = about -1.28. That matches the reported -1.257 within rounding. Reject is correct."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "After the two-stage XGBoost fit, drop the 5% of training molecules with the largest in-sample absolute residuals, refit both stages on the remainder with the same params, and predict with the refit model while the ridge base stays fit on all data.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "pine", "idea_id": "b029", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_caco_HH_1_s0-candidate-14_1795047162206", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00186804, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00186804, "latency_s": 6.133056580030825, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7011, "tokens_out": 1458}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.036871799999999996, "cost_usd_plan": 0.036871799999999996, "latency_s": 15.8200793970027, "requested_model": "opus", "role": "critic", "served_model": "opus", "tokens_in": 2584, "tokens_out": 1356}], "official_val_bpb": 0.3712508780204336, "sealed_val_bpb": null, "slot"